      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we start by analyzing the given information:\n\n1. Each man danced with exactly three women.\n2. Each woman danced with exactly two men.\n3. There were 12 men at the party.\n\nLet's denote the number of women by \\( w \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of \"man-woman\" dance pairs. Since each man danced with 3 women, and there are 12 men, the total number of dance pairs involving men is:\n\\[\n12 \\times 3 = 36\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total number of \"man-woman\" dance pairs involving women. Since each woman danced with 2 men, and there are \\( w \\) women, the total number of dance pairs involving women is:\n\\[\nw \\times 2\n\\]\n\nSince each dance pair is counted once for each man and once for each woman, the total number of dance pairs (man-woman pairs) is the same in both calculations. Therefore, we set the two expressions equal to each other:\n\\[\nw \\times 2 = 36\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( w \\), we solve the equation:\n\\[\nw = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
