      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we can use the information given about the number of men and the number of women who danced with them.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - Each man danced with exactly 3 women.\n   - Each woman danced with exactly 2 men.\n   - There were 12 men at the party.\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of dances involving men:**\n   Since each of the 12 men danced with 3 women, the total number of dances involving men is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 3 = 36\n   \\]\n   This means that 36 dances were formed by the men.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of dances involving women:**\n   Since each of the \\( w \\) women danced with 2 men, the total number of dances involving women is:\n   \\[\n   2w\n   \\]\n   (Note that each dance involves one man and one woman, so the total number of dances is the product of the number of men and the number of women).\n\n4. **Set up the equation:**\n   Since the total number of dances involving men is equal to the total number of dances involving women, we can set up the following equation:\n   \\[\n   2w = 36\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\( w \\):**\n   \\[\n   w = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
